# QuantTerminal Pro 📈

A Bloomberg-style financial dashboard with live market data, AI-powered stock analysis, portfolio tracking, and quantitative risk tools — built with Python + vanilla HTML/CSS/JS.

![QuantTerminal Screenshot](screenshot.png)

## ✨ Features

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| **Live Market Data** | Real-time prices via yfinance — US, India (NSE/BSE), UK, Crypto, Forex, Commodities |
| **Interactive Charts** | Price chart (1D/5D/1M/6M) with RSI(14) indicator overlay |
| **Portfolio Tracker** | Add holdings, track live P&L, export to CSV |
| **DCF Valuation** | Discounted Cash Flow calculator with WACC, growth assumptions, and intrinsic value |
| **Risk Metrics** | VaR (1D/1W, 95%), Sharpe Ratio, Sortino Ratio, Beta, Max Drawdown |
| **Monte Carlo** | 500 simulated price paths over 30 trading days |
| **Efficient Frontier** | Markowitz MPT — 800 random portfolios, max Sharpe highlighted |
| **Stress Testing** | Historical crash scenarios (2008 GFC, COVID, 2022) via beta sensitivity |
| **SMA Backtesting** | Configurable SMA crossover strategy on 2 years of data |
| **News Feed** | Latest headlines per stock via Yahoo Finance |
| **AI Audit** | Google Gemini-powered bull/bear analysis of selected stock |
| **Mobile Responsive** | Works on phone, tablet, and desktop |

## 🛠 Tech Stack

- **Backend**: Python 3.x · Flask · yfinance · gunicorn
- **Frontend**: Vanilla HTML/CSS/JavaScript (no frameworks)
- **Data**: Yahoo Finance public API via yfinance
- **AI**: Google Gemini 1.5 Flash (user provides own API key)
- **Deployment**: Railway.app

## ⚡ Quick Start (Local)

### 1. Clone the repo
```bash
git clone https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/quant-terminal.git
cd quant-terminal
```

### 2. Install Python dependencies
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 3. Start the backend
```bash
python server.py
```
You should see:
```
QuantTerminal Backend → http://localhost:5000
```

### 4. Open the dashboard
Open `index.html` in VS Code → right-click → **Open with Live Server**

Or just drag `index.html` into Chrome.

## 🌐 Deployment (Railway)

See **DEPLOY.md** for full step-by-step Railway deployment guide.

Live URL: **https://YOUR-APP.railway.app**

## 🔍 How to Use

### Search
Type any ticker in the search bar:
- `AAPL` — US stock
- `RELIANCE.NS` — Indian NSE stock
- `BARC.L` — UK LSE stock
- `BTC-USD` — Cryptocurrency
- `EURUSD=X` — Forex pair
- `GC=F` — Gold futures

### AI Audit
Go to the **AI Audit** tab → enter your Google Gemini API key (free at [aistudio.google.com](https://aistudio.google.com)) → click Run. Your key is never stored.

### DCF Valuation
Go to **DCF** tab → select a stock → adjust WACC and growth assumptions → click Calculate. The tool shows intrinsic value vs current price with full year-by-year breakdown.

## ⚠️ Limitations & Disclaimers

- Uses Yahoo Finance public API via yfinance — data may be delayed
- **Not a production trading system** — no order execution
- No transaction costs, slippage, or taxes in backtesting
- DCF is highly sensitive to WACC (±1% = ±15% valuation change)
- Risk metrics (VaR, Sharpe) use simplified estimates
- AI audit may contain inaccuracies — always verify independently
- **This is not investment advice**

